1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,900
An AML alert is a question, not a conclusion.

2
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:10,500
SignalFlow is a synthetic-data investigation prototype for the Global AI Hackathon's
AI Agents and Intelligent Systems challenge.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,300
Every record, score, and event in this workspace is fictional.

4
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:16,100
Open the sample case.

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:19,700
Its score prioritizes review. It does not establish wrongdoing.

6
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:26,100
For this verified run, the bounded agent uses GPT-6.1 Sol
through the current Manus model gateway.

7
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:31,900
Its only tools read synthetic signals, identify missing context,
and retrieve a sample review checklist.

8
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:34,700
Here is the live tool trace returned by the server.

9
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:38,300
The model drafts a next step, but an analyst owns the decision.

10
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:42,300
The agent cannot access a bank system, search the web, or change a case.

11
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:45,200
This video verifies one synthetic-case run.

12
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:48,200
It does not prove AML performance or production readiness.

13
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:52,500
The public GitHub Pages site remains deterministic and makes no model call.

14
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:56,400
The agent runs locally with an explicitly configured compatible provider.

15
00:00:56,400 --> 00:01:01,400
SignalFlow's original interface began in the separate
Azentio AI Build Labs project.

16
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:04,800
The bounded agent adaptation was added for the Global AI Hackathon.

17
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:06,300
That history is disclosed.
